		"meta": {
			"author": "",
			"category": "source",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 23,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Geo Tiles - tile collage of flat geometric motifs in three colors, 67 motifs: rows and grids (triangles, chevrons, waves, scales, quarter- and half-circle truchets, triangle truchets, bricks, windows, dots, rings, crosses, drops, diamonds, herringbone, plaid, sunbursts, rainbow rings, concentric squares) with single accent elements; combined tiles of mini motifs; strewn quartered circles, leaves on a stem; figures (trees, flowers, tulips, birds, fish, butterflies, stars, moons, suns, houses, mushrooms, clouds, mountains, eyes, spirals, pinwheels, arches, domes, hearts, drops ...). Per tile: motif, zoom (patterns from fine texture to a few big cropped shapes; figures from small to big crops), placement, rotation, mirror and colors. Nothing moves by itself. Columns \/ Rows: tile grid, set separately. Seed: whole numbers, each value is a new layout; changes cut hard. Fill (%): share of tiles shown; fixed rank per tile, raising Fill only adds tiles (FFT friendly). Big Tiles (%): share of 2x2 blocks merged into 2x2, 2x1 or 1x2 tiles. Motion: Animate (%) = share of tiles that follow Pattern Shift (fixed rank per tile, 0 = nothing moves, 100 = all tiles). Pattern Shift 0 to 1 = one loop: patterns travel 8 elements (direction per tile), figures turn once, pulse or bob 4 times; a 0-1 loop is seamless (e.g. BPM Sync 16 beats). Figures with an up direction never rotate. Color 1-3: each tile uses all three colors as background, shape and accent. Backdrop On\/Off: empty tiles show the backdrop color or stay transparent. Drawn by the ISF shader GeoTiles.fs in the patch folder (must stay next to the patch).",
			"displayName": "Geo Tiles",
			"identifier": "1a89845f-dffa-4ac8-a147-f9e2d6630754",
			"licenseName": "",
			"mail": "",
